Despite manpage comments describing how you can swap to a file, you can't.
You can only swap to a partition.

"eager" vs "lazy" -
"Eager" allocation is performed when the address space is created. 
"Lazy"  allocation is performed when you're about to swap.
In most cases, lazy allocation consumes less swap space - at a cost of
processes getting killed when they try to swap but can't allocate any more
swap space.
	-Rick
