DEC OSF/1 AXP 1.2 is available for DEC Alpha AXP
workstations.  It will also be available for DEC's
Alpha AXP "PC" shortly after Windows NT is launched.

Digital has no plans to port the OSF/1 operating
system to other platforms.  Specifically, DEC no
longer plans to port OSF/1 to MIPS RISC workstations.

The OSF organization ported the reference version of
OSF/1 to an Intel 386/486 platform.  However, no
OSF licensee has announced production of an O.S.
for the Intel machines.  IBM has disclosed plans to
employ the OSF microkernel based on Mach 3.0 
as the host for a system that could run either OS/2
or AIX.  This would not be OSF/1, which is based on
the Mach 2.5 microkernel.

So far, only DEC has announced a commercial OSF/1.
Anybody know any different?

