There were three reference platforms for OSF/1 (i.e., the integrated
kernel version based on Mach 2.5), Encore Multimax, Digital DECstation
2100/3100, and Intel 386. I don't know whether that is the case OSF/1
MK (i.e., the microkernel version based on Mach 3.0). The Intel
386/486 may be the only reference platform for OSF/1 MK. Possibly
someone from OSF might take a moment to comment...

>   OSF licensee has announced production of an O.S.
>   for the Intel machines.  IBM has disclosed plans to
